		summary = "The **Banc d'Arguin National Park** of Bay of Arguin lies in Western Africa on the west coast of [[Mauritania]] between [[Nouakchott]] and Nouadhibou and is the former mouth of the Tamanrasset River. The [[World Heritage Site]] is a major site for [[Bird migration|migratory]] [[Bird|birds]] and breeding birds, including [[Flamingo|flamingos]], [[Pelican|pelicans]] and [[Tern|terns]]. Much of the breeding is on sand banks including the islands of Tidra, Niroumi, Nair, Kijji and Arguim. The surrounding waters are some of the richest fishing waters in western Africa and serve as nesting grounds for the entire western region.",
